# ── Local TLS certs for on-device HTTPS dev (SKYMAP_HTTPS=1) ──────────────────
# mkcert-generated leaf cert + private key for serving the dev server over
# HTTPS to a phone/tablet on the LAN (see vite.config.ts). Machine-local and
# secret — the key must never be committed. Regenerate via:
#   mkdir -p .certs && cd .certs && mkcert <lan-ip> localhost
.certs/

# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# Python venv used by the maintainer-only MCPM extractor (data/raw/mcpm/README.md).
# Local-only; recreate via `python3 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install ...`.
.venv/
__pycache__/

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vite ships compiled assets into dist/ and a transient cache into .vite/.
# TypeScript's incremental-build state lives in *.tsbuildinfo files.
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Test artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/
.vitest-cache/
# Playwright per-run output: failure screenshots, traces, and HTML reports.
# Regenerated on every `npx playwright test` invocation; not useful to track.
test-results/
playwright-report/
# Playwright's per-machine `.cache/` lives outside the repo (in
# ~/Library/Caches/ms-playwright on macOS), so we don't need to ignore it.

# ── Environment files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default-deny `.env*` keeps secrets out by accident.  The carve-out below
# is `.env.production`: it carries `VITE_DATA_BASE_URL`, the public R2 URL
# the runtime fetcher uses (visible to anyone in DevTools' network tab —
# not a secret).  We tried two cleaner alternatives — Cloudflare's dashboard
# "Variables and Secrets" panel, and wrangler.toml [vars] — and verified
# empirically that neither is exposed to the build environment for Workers
# Assets projects: a `process.env.VITE_DATA_BASE_URL` console.log inside
# vite.config.ts logged `null` in both cases.  Vite *only* picks the value
# up via `.env*` files at the repo root, so the file has to ship in git
# for the prod bundle to inline the URL.
#
# Anything genuinely secret (API tokens, write-credentials) should still go
# through `npx wrangler secret put` — those don't show up in this file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.production

# ── OS clutter ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ── Editor / IDE state ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# JetBrains (.idea) and VS Code (.vscode) directories carry per-user state we
# don't want shared.  Some `.idea/*.xml` files were accidentally committed
# earlier in the project's history; new files won't be tracked, but those
# already-tracked files stay in git until removed explicitly via
# `git rm --cached .idea/<file>`.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── Catalog data (bulky, externally sourced or rebuildable) ───────────────────
# Top-level `/data/` holds the raw downloaded catalog files (2MRS, GLADE,
# SDSS CSV exports), the per-survey `.bin` build artefacts, and small
# `sample.*` fixtures used by ad-hoc dev scripts.  At ~880 MB it is far
# too large for git and is fully reproducible by re-running the parsers
# under tools/ on freshly downloaded source files.
#
# Leading `/` anchors the rule to the repo root so it does NOT match
# `src/data/` (TypeScript source) or `tests/data/` (test fixtures and
# unit tests).  An unanchored `data/` would silently swallow new files
# in those directories — see the implementer's note on Task 1 of the
# colour-index plan, which hit exactly that trap.
/data/

# Exception: hand-curated catalog seed files (small, hand-authored, tracked).
!/data/famous_galaxies.seed.json

# Exception: hand-curated override index produced by the famous-galaxy
# curator (tools/famous-curator).  Small JSON (~75 entries × ~150 B) that
# overrides the auto-fetched Wikipedia/DESI thumbnails per-galaxy; must
# ship in git so a fresh clone + `npm run fetch-famous-images` honours
# the curated picks.  See docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-18-famous-galaxy-
# curator-design.md "Override index" for the schema.
!/data/famous_curated_overrides.json

# Exception: font sources for the MSDF label atlas. Third-party OFL-licensed
# assets, not rebuildable by our parsers — they're the upstream input to
# `npm run build-fonts`, same conceptual role as the seed JSON above.
!/data/raw/fonts/CormorantGaramond-SemiBold.ttf

# Exception: CF-4 raw-data README.  The directory holds gitignored
# intermediates (`.sav`, `.npy`, `.meta.json`) that are too large or too
# maintainer-specific to track, but the README documents how contributors
# obtain them from R2 — so the README itself must be checked in even
# though everything around it is ignored.
!/data/raw/cf4/README.md

# Exception: CF-4 distance-table checksum sidecar.  The 100 MB table2.dat
# itself stays gitignored, but the .sha256 lets the parser detect a
# truncated or stale download — pinning it in git makes that check
# tamper-evident and lets contributors verify their fetch matches.
!/data/raw/cf4/table2.dat.sha256

# Exception: MCPM Cosmic Web raw-data README — same rationale as the
# CF-4 README above.  Intermediates (`.npy`, `.bin.bz2`) are gitignored
# but the README must be checked in so contributors know how to fetch
# them from R2.
!/data/raw/mcpm/README.md

# Exception: Milliquas raw-data README — same rationale as the CF-4 and
# MCPM READMEs above.  The catalog itself (`milliquas.txt` ~194 MB,
# `milliquas.zip` ~32 MB, plus ReadMe / references / sample sidecars) is
# gitignored; contributors populate it via `npm run fetch-milliquas`.
!/data/raw/milliquas/README.md

# `public/data/` is the Vite-served copy of the built `.bin` files (~100 MB).
# Generated by `npm run build:bins` (or equivalent) — never hand-edited.
/public/data/

# 2MASS XSC PA/axis-ratio cache fetched by `npm run fetch-2mass-xsc`. Already
# covered by `/data/` above, but listed explicitly so future readers see it
# alongside the other catalog artefacts. ~1 MB of tabular data; rebuildable.
data/raw/2mass_xsc_pa.csv
data/raw/hyperleda_pa.csv

# StarNet++ model weights used by the famous-galaxy curator (tools/famous-
# curator).  Hundreds of MB of binary weights, license-restricted by
# upstream — too large and too restricted for git.  Curator users install
# them locally and point STARNET_WEIGHTS at the directory.  Already
# covered by `/data/` above; listed explicitly so future readers don't
# accidentally check them in.
data/starnet/

# ── Claude Code per-developer state ───────────────────────────────────────────
# `settings.local.json` accumulates this developer's locally-granted tool
# permissions; the shared `settings.json` (when it exists) stays tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# `.claude/worktrees/` holds the actual git worktree checkouts spawned by
# EnterWorktree / `git worktree add` — each is a full working copy of the
# repo, not shared state.  They must never be committed (a stray `git add
# .claude/` would otherwise try to vacuum entire checkouts into the tree).
.claude/worktrees/

# ── Source video recordings under docs/screenshots/ ─────────────────────────
# QuickTime / CleanShot drops a .mov per recording.  We commit the encoded
# `.gif` and `.png` artefacts (referenced from README.md) but never the raw
# video — they're 50–100 MB each, regenerable from the recording session,
# and would inflate the clone size for no playback benefit on github.com.
docs/screenshots/*.mov
docs/screenshots/*.mp4

# ── Firebase CLI per-developer cache ─────────────────────────────────────────
# `.firebase/hosting.*.cache` records the previously-deployed file hashes so
# `firebase deploy` can skip files whose content hasn't changed.  The cache
# is regenerated on every deploy and is per-developer state, not shared.
.firebase/

# ── Outreach drafts (personal voice + recipient strategy, local-only) ─────────
# The per-item post and email drafts under `posts-and-emails/` carry the
# author's personal voice samples, recipient connection notes, and "TO VERIFY"
# blockers that don't belong in the public repo.  The plan-level summary
# files (task-4-public-posts.md, task-5-academic-emails.md) stay tracked and
# point at the local-only files.
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-05-outreach-and-promotion/posts-and-emails/

# Standalone outreach email drafts.  Same rationale as the
# posts-and-emails/ directory above — recipient-specific drafts,
# unsent voice samples, and TO-VERIFY notes that don't belong in
# the public repo.
docs/outreach/emails/

# Brainstorming companion mockup HTML + state files.  Generated by the
# superpowers `brainstorming` skill when sketching design options
# visually.  Worth keeping on disk per-session as reference (designers
# may want to look back at the mockups that led to a spec), but
# committing them would leak transient mockups into the repo.
docs/brainstorm/

# CF-4 DM density cube intermediates (gitignored — hosted on R2; see data/raw/cf4/README.md)
data/raw/cf4/*.sav
data/raw/cf4/*.npy
data/raw/cf4/*.meta.json

# MCPM Cosmic Web cube intermediates and build artefacts (gitignored —
# .npy tiers hosted on R2; .scfd outputs are deterministic build outputs.
# See data/raw/mcpm/README.md.)
data/raw/mcpm/*.npy
data/raw/mcpm/*.bin.bz2
public/data/mcpm-*.scfd
.superpowers/
